# Vercel CLI upload exclusions.
#
# IMPORTANT — why this file exists and why it must mirror .gitignore.
#
# `vercel deploy` uploads files from the LOCAL WORKING DIRECTORY, not from the
# Git repository. When this file is absent, the CLI falls back to including
# everything it finds on disk apart from a small built-in default list, and it
# does NOT consult .gitignore. That is how the deliberately removed founder
# photograph (public/images/founder/farzana-tabussum.jpg) was published at a
# guessable URL on the live site despite being correctly excluded from Git.
#
# When .vercelignore exists it is the ONLY ignore file the CLI honours, so every
# exclusion that matters must be listed here as well as in .gitignore. Keeping
# the two in step is a manual responsibility; .gitignore governs the repository
# and this file governs what is uploaded to Vercel.

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
dist/

# Vercel's own local state
.vercel/

# Environment — never upload real values
.env*
!.env.example

# The founder photograph, deliberately removed from the site. Nothing in src/
# references it; excluding it here is what keeps it off the deployed host.
public/images/founder/
Farzana_Tabussum.jpeg

# Verification scratch: screenshots, sweep logs, ad-hoc test scripts
.work/

# Build-irrelevant source material
CamScanner *.pdf

# Local machine artefacts
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
